@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture;motion] kit-decides-the-way
Which way a page, tab, file or label moves is decided in the kit, never by a screen:
`BlurSwitch`, `LabelSwitch` and `rememberPageSlide` take an `order` and work the way out
with `pageWay`, and Back goes through `PageBack`. A kit slide MUST take its offset from
the way (rule 105; motion check).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:motion] kit-drags-carry-on-or-settle
A page, row or sheet let go after a drag settles back where it was or carries on the way
the finger went, at the speed it was thrown; it never springs toward the start first. A
throw of 500dp/s counts as a swipe once the finger has taken the page part of the way, so
a nudge never turns a page by itself (L6, `kit-side-pages-slide-whole`), and a throw back
against the drag cancels it (rule 105).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:motion] kit-side-pages-slide-whole
`SidePages` and `FilePages` move pages that sit side by side the whole width with
nothing fading or blurring, both pages in view while they move, and settle on
`PullsMotion.PageSpring`, critically damped with no snap at the end (rule 107; H20, H36,
J7). The Overview's pages are drawn before the first drag, so the first swipe from Summary
to Conversation moves as smoothly as the way back and never pops or holds at its start
(recording 16 Oct 09:50, 03:29 to 03:53; M8). A page moves exactly as far as the finger, and a quick flick turns the page only once
the finger has moved it part of the way, so a page never "swipes by itself" (recording
15 Oct 15:37, 04:12 to 04:31; L6).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] kit-side-pages-keep-state
A page held by `SidePages` keeps its scroll and saved state while another page is on
screen, and finds them again when it comes back (rule 118; J9).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:motion] kit-tab-ink-follows-the-pages
The underline of `UnderlineTabs` is one stroke that slides between labels in 250ms and,
while a finger drags the pages, sits where the pages are on that frame (rule 105; J15).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:motion] kit-segment-highlight-slides
In `CapsuleTabs` the highlight slides to the tapped segment instead of jumping, and the
new content fades in (rule 67).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:motion;design] kit-press-only-tints
Pressing a row, tile, card or sheet row tints it while held and nothing else: no scale,
no shift, no ripple. Small controls (round buttons, pills, chips, the send circle) MAY
keep their 0.97 press (rule 82; F71).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:design] kit-edges-fade
Content that scrolls under anything pinned (a header, chips, a sheet's header, the Tour
strip, the bottom pill, the Diff's counts line) fades to the page colour with a blur made
from content past the edge; it never ends in a hard line, is never stretched, and the
pinned thing itself stays sharp (rule 74; F2, F57).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:design] kit-sideways-scroll-fades
Anything that scrolls sideways (the branch row, chips, a code block, a table) fades at an
edge it can still scroll toward and stays sharp at an edge with nothing past it
(`sideScrollFade`, rule 74; J14, J23).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:motion] kit-skeletons-shimmer
Every skeleton bar shimmers: a soft band about 40% of its width sweeps left to right every
1200ms in light and dark. A skeleton that does not move is a defect; with "Remove
animations" on it sits still (rule 85; F42, F66).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:design] kit-floating-things-cast-the-canvas-shadow
Every floating element (round header buttons, the search pill, bars, cards, menus) carries
`floatShadow` at its level: a soft ink drop pushed down, with the tight edge layer, never
an even glow. A missing or different shadow is a defect (rule 45).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:design] kit-same-control-on-page-and-sheet
One kind of control looks the same on a page and in a sheet: a sheet's close and back
buttons are the round white button with its shadow, and its segmented controls are the
Inbox capsule (rule 70).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:motion] kit-menus-and-dialogs-move
Menus grow out of their trigger and dialogs scale in, with rule 73's numbers: 150ms for
closes and text swaps, 250ms for opens and tabs, 400ms for panels, one smooth-out curve
(rules 59 and 73).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:design] kit-one-markdown
All Markdown in the app (AI text, changelogs, rules, contracts) is drawn by the kit's
`Markdown`, so a mention, a cite and a code span look and behave the same everywhere.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:design] kit-icons-from-lu
Icons come from `Lu` (Lucide, a published set) and the brand marks; no icon is drawn by
hand in a screen, and the same icon never appears twice on one card (rule 48).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:design] kit-dark-is-neutral-grey
In dark mode every surface is a grey whose red, green and blue differ by at most 2, the
accent stays teal, and every colour token has a dark pair (rule 76; F13).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:design] kit-teal-is-the-darker-one
The Overview's Review and the Diff's round › take `primary`, the darker teal Tavi kept
over the canvas's brighter one (D2).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] kit-copy-shows-a-toast
Copying shows the dark toast and leaves the copied control unchanged (rule 83; F21).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;design] kit-picking-lists-search
A sheet that picks from a list (themes, earlier chats, models) has a search over it once the
list is long. The plain lists (themes, earlier chats) are the one `SearchList` component, and
its groups keep the list's order; the model list, which lists older models under a heading and splits Pi's by
provider, uses the same `SheetSearch` and matching ("most bottom sheets that we have actually
benefit a lot from search", recording 15 Oct 15:37, 12:26 to 12:36; L4, L23, L36).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:design] kit-fold-headings-line-up
Every fold heading on a page reads "Name (count) ⌄": the count in parentheses right after
the name and the chevron right after the count, on the name's line whatever its length (a
long name gives way at its end), and the hairline under it ("these chevrons are not
aligned", recording 15 Oct 15:37, 08:05 to 08:21; L3, L12). Anything else a heading
carries, such as a section's + and −, sits at its right edge in the same fixed columns as
the rows' numbers, so the numbers of a list line up. Tavi decided this in the recording of
16 Oct 12:10, 00:08 to 00:47, 14:57 and 18:03 to 18:21 ("those two are rules"; N1, N35),
replacing the count and chevron at the right edge. Sheets have no fold headings
(kit-sheet-headings).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:design] kit-sheet-headings
Every bottom sheet heads its sections with the one `SheetHeading`, the small muted heading
of the Settings sheet: no line under it, no count and no chevron, and nothing folds. Checks,
Commits, Files, the model list and the rest use it ("it has to be the same logic everywhere",
recording 16 Oct 09:50, 02:55 to 03:27 and 03:54 to 04:05; M7, Tavi's decision, replacing
the fold headings of L12 on sheets). A sheet's first field sits `SheetTopGap` under the ✕,
more than before (M7).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:design] kit-tab-marks-sit-centred
A capsule tab's mark and word sit centred in the tab with room either side; a word too long
for it ends in an ellipsis and never wraps out of sight (recording 15 Oct 15:37, 11:50 to
12:07; L22).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:design;product] kit-pictures-are-sharp-and-open
A picture in Markdown is drawn from a load at the screen's density, as sharp as on GitHub,
and a tap on it opens its link, or the picture itself, never what is under the text
(recording 15 Oct 15:37, 09:10 to 09:28; L14, L15).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:design;architecture] kit-one-text-field
Every place that takes typing is built on the kit's one field, `FieldText`, and a framed
one on `FieldFrame`: one height, one inner padding, one text style, the placeholder in the
muted ink in that same style, and the teal cursor. A field at the bottom of a page is the
pill; a search on a sheet has the cards' corner and shadow and sits `SheetTopGap` under
the ✕ (Commands too). The ✕ that clears a field sits the same distance from its end
everywhere. No screen calls Compose's `BasicTextField` or `TextField` itself; the bans check
holds the remaining ones to a baseline that only shrinks. Tavi asked for this in the
recording of 16 Oct 12:10, 03:23 to 04:03 and 15:10 to 15:36 ("go through the entire
project and standardize this stuff"; N6).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:design] kit-fields-fade-where-text-hides
Where a field's text has scrolled out of sight, it fades into the field at that edge: at
the start or end of a one-line field, at the top or bottom of one that scrolls through
lines. An edge with nothing hidden past it has no fade, and the fade grows with how far the
text has scrolled. Tavi asked for this in the recording of 16 Oct 12:10, 05:47 to 06:00
(fade both ways, sideways and up and down; N9).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:design] kit-bottom-bars-rest-alike
Every bar at the foot of a page or a sheet (the Inbox's and a repository's search, the
Overview's and the Tour's Ask bars, the diff's file bar, a full sheet's footer) MUST take
its place from the kit's one `floatingBar` modifier: 16dp in from the sides and the same
lift over the navigation bar, rising with the keyboard. A page MUST NOT set its own
bottom padding for its bar, so opening a pull request never moves the bar ("the placement
of the search and bottom bars and the buttons ... should be consistent throughout all of
them", recording of 17 Oct 13:26, 00:49 to 01:26, P3; rule 192).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:design;motion;architecture] kit-one-foot-bar
The search and Ask bars MUST be one pill, `FootPill`, drawn once over the pages by
`FootBarLayer` in the app's root; a page says what the pill holds and MUST NOT draw a pill
of its own. Going from one page to another keeps the pill in place and changes only what is
inside it, the words fading out blurred and the next ones in, its width easing to the new
page's; a button beside it leaves or arrives with its page, and the diff's file bar takes
its place through `FootFree` ("one component that's kind of over the screen, and then we
can swap the text inside it with that nice blur fade ... we want that kind of seamlessness
when we go into a PR as well", recording 17 Oct 14:45, 01:00 to 01:51; Q2; rule 196).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] kit-foot-bar-owns-its-taps
A tap anywhere on the foot pill, its edge and padding included, MUST open it or put the
cursor in its field, and MUST NOT reach the page under it ("I keep trying to tap on the
ask about this pull request, and it keeps getting me to the description", recording
17 Oct 14:45, 03:00 to 03:10; Q6; rule 198).
